{"ansatz.py": "\"\"\"Stage A: concentric-shrink ansatz for a near-6-colouring of the plane.\n\nStart from the standard 7-colouring by regular hexagons of side s (2s<1,\nsame-colour separation sqrt(21)s-2s>1).  Delete colour 7.  Each colour-7\nhexagon H is cut into 6 trapezoids (between its side and a concentric inner\nhexagon of side t) plus the inner hexagon; the trapezoid adjacent to the\nside shared with the colour-c neighbour is given to colour c.  Wild set =\ninner hexagons, density p = (t/s)^2 / 7.\n\nConstraints for colour class c = T_c + Lambda (Lambda hexagonal lattice of\nminimal norm sqrt(21)s):\n   (D) diam(T_c) <= 1          (tiles are taken open; boundary points are\n                                assigned to any adjacent tile, a null set)\n   (S) dist(T_c, T_c + lam) >= 1 for lam in Lambda minus 0\nBoth are checked exactly (polygon vertex/edge distances) with sympy-free\nfloating point at 1e-12 tolerance, then the optimal (s,t) is bisected.\n\"\"\"\nimport math, itertools\nimport numpy as np\nfrom shapely.geometry import Polygon\nfrom shapely import affinity\n\ndef hexagon(center, side, phase=math.pi/6):\n    cx, cy = center\n    return [(cx + side*math.cos(phase + k*math.pi/3), cy + side*math.sin(phase + k*math.pi/3)) for k in range(6)]\n\ndef tile(s, t):\n    \"\"\"Colour-1 tile: hexagon centred at a=(sqrt3 s,0) plus trapezoid of wild hexagon at 0.\"\"\"\n    a = (math.sqrt(3)*s, 0.0)\n    hexa = hexagon(a, s)\n    # wild hexagon at origin; its right side is x = sqrt3 s/2, from angle -30 to 30 deg\n    outer = [(s*math.cos(-math.pi/6), s*math.sin(-math.pi/6)), (s*math.cos(math.pi/6), s*math.sin(math.pi/6))]\n    inner = [(t*math.cos(math.pi/6), t*math.sin(math.pi/6)), (t*math.cos(-math.pi/6), t*math.sin(-math.pi/6))]\n    # hexa vertices: k=0..5 at angles 30+60k about a; the left side is between k=2 (150deg) and k=3 (210deg)\n    # walk hexagon k=3,4,5,0,1,2 then the two inner points (inner[0] is upper, inner[1] lower)\n    pts = [hexa[3], hexa[4], hexa[5], hexa[0], hexa[1], hexa[2], inner[0], inner[1]]\n    if t >= s - 1e-15:\n        pts = hexa\n    P = Polygon(pts)\n    assert P.is_valid, (s, t)\n    return P\n\ndef lattice(s, rng=2):\n    th = math.atan(math.sqrt(3)/5)  # direction of 2a+b, a=(sqrt3 s,0), b=(sqrt3 s/2, 3s/2)\n    L = math.sqrt(21)*s\n    g1 = np.array([L*math.cos(th), L*math.sin(th)])\n    g2 = np.array([L*math.cos(th+math.pi/3), L*math.sin(th+math.pi/3)])\n    return [tuple(i*g1 + j*g2) for i in range(-rng, rng+1) for j in range(-rng, rng+1) if (i, j) != (0, 0)]\n\ndef diam(poly):\n    pts = list(poly.exterior.coords)\n    return max(math.dist(p, q) for p, q in itertools.combinations(pts, 2))\n\ndef min_sep(poly, s):\n    return min(poly.distance(affinity.translate(poly, *lam)) for lam in lattice(s))\n\ndef feasible(s, t, tol=1e-12):\n    T = tile(s, t)\n    return diam(T) <= 1 + tol and min_sep(T, s) >= 1 - tol\n\ndef wild_density(s, t):\n    return (t/s)**2 / 7\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # sanity: t = s gives the plain 6-of-7 colouring, p = 1/7\n    best = None\n    for s in np.linspace(0.35, 0.5, 301):\n        # smallest feasible t for this s (bisection; feasibility is monotone in t)\n        if not feasible(s, s):\n            continue\n        lo, hi = 0.0, s\n        if feasible(s, 0.0):\n            hi = 0.0\n        else:\n            for _ in range(60):\n                mid = (lo+hi)/2\n                if feasible(s, mid): hi = mid\n                else: lo = mid\n        p = wild_density(s, hi)\n        if best is None or p < best[0]:\n            best = (p, s, hi)\n    p, s, t = best\n    T = tile(s, t)\n    print(f\"best ansatz: s={s:.6f} t={t:.6f} t/s={t/s:.6f} p={p:.6e} 1/p={1/p:.1f}\")\n    print(f\"  diam={diam(T):.12f} sep={min_sep(T,s):.12f}\")\n", "optimize.py": "\"\"\"Stage B: parametrised local search over periodic 6-colourings with 6-fold symmetry.\n\nAnsatz: colour classes C_k = R^k T + Lambda, k=0..5, where R = rotation by 60 deg\nabout the origin, Lambda = hexagonal lattice of minimal norm L (free), and T is a\nsimple polygon with n free vertices.  Wild set W = plane minus union of classes.\n\nHard constraints (penalised):\n  (D) diam(T) <= 1\n  (S) dist(T, T+lam) >= 1 for lam in Lambda minus 0 (|lam| <= 2L suffices when L<=... checked over range 2)\n  (X) area(T cap (R^j T + lam)) = 0 for (j,lam) != (0,0), |lam| small\n  (V) T simple (valid polygon)\nObjective: minimise wild density p = 1 - 6 area(T) / (sqrt3/2 L^2).\n\nOptimiser: Nelder-Mead on penalised objective, restarted with random perturbations\n(coordinate descent style), from the Stage-A ansatz tile with subdivided edges.\nFinal answer is re-checked with tolerance 1e-9 and the polygon is written to JSON.\n\"\"\"\nimport math, itertools, json, sys, time\nimport numpy as np\nfrom shapely.geometry import Polygon\nfrom shapely import affinity\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nfrom ansatz import tile as ansatz_tile\n\nSQ3 = math.sqrt(3)\n\nTH = math.atan(SQ3/5)  # 7-colouring lattice direction relative to tile centre a=(sqrt3 s,0)\ndef LATT(L):\n    return (np.array([L*math.cos(TH), L*math.sin(TH)]), np.array([L*math.cos(TH+math.pi/3), L*math.sin(TH+math.pi/3)]))\n\ndef lattice_vecs(L, rng):\n    g1, g2 = LATT(L)\n    return [i*g1 + j*g2 for i in range(-rng, rng+1) for j in range(-rng, rng+1) if (i, j) != (0, 0)]\n\ndef rot(P, k):\n    return affinity.rotate(P, 60*k, origin=(0, 0))\n\ndef diam(P):\n    pts = list(P.exterior.coords)[:-1]\n    return max(math.dist(p, q) for p, q in itertools.combinations(pts, 2))\n\ndef constraints(P, L):\n    \"\"\"returns (diam, min separation, max overlap area)\"\"\"\n    d = diam(P)\n    sep = min([P.distance(affinity.translate(P, *lam)) for lam in lattice_vecs(L, 2) if np.linalg.norm(lam) < 1 + d + 1e-9], default=10.0)\n    ov = 0.0\n    for j in range(1, 6):\n        Q = rot(P, j)\n        for lam in [np.zeros(2)] + lattice_vecs(L, 2):\n            if np.linalg.norm(lam) > 3.0: continue\n            ov = max(ov, P.intersection(affinity.translate(Q, *lam)).area)\n    return d, sep, ov\n\ndef wild(P, L):\n    return 1 - 6*P.area / (SQ3/2 * L**2)\n\ndef unpack(x):\n    L = x[0]\n    pts = x[1:].reshape(-1, 2)\n    return L, pts\n\ndef penalised(x, w=1e4):\n    L, pts = unpack(x)\n    P = Polygon(pts)\n    if not P.is_valid or P.area <= 0 or L <= 0:\n        return 10.0\n    d, sep, ov = constraints(P, L)\n    pen = max(0, d-1)**2 + max(0, 1-sep)**2 + ov\n    return wild(P, L) + w*pen\n\ndef subdivide(pts, k):\n    out = []\n    n = len(pts)\n    for i in range(n):\n        a, b = np.array(pts[i]), np.array(pts[(i+1) % n])\n        for t in range(k):\n            out.append(tuple(a + (b-a)*t/k))\n    return out\n\ndef run(seed=0, n_sub=2, iters=6, s=0.4365, t=0.218475, verbose=True):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    P0 = ansatz_tile(s, t)\n    pts = subdivide(list(P0.exterior.coords)[:-1], n_sub)\n    L = math.sqrt(21)*s\n    x = np.concatenate([[L], np.array(pts).ravel()])\n    best = penalised(x)\n    if verbose: print(f\"start p_pen={best:.6f} wild={wild(Polygon(pts),L):.6f}\")\n    for it in range(iters):\n        res = minimize(penalised, x, method='Nelder-Mead', options=dict(maxiter=4000, xatol=1e-7, fatol=1e-10, adaptive=True))\n        if res.fun < best:\n            best, x = res.fun, res.x\n        # random kick\n        xk = x + rng.normal(scale=0.003, size=x.shape) * (np.arange(len(x)) > 0)\n        res = minimize(penalised, xk, method='Nelder-Mead', options=dict(maxiter=4000, xatol=1e-7, fatol=1e-10, adaptive=True))\n        if res.fun < best:\n            best, x = res.fun, res.x\n        if verbose:\n            L, pts = unpack(x); P = Polygon(pts)\n            print(f\"iter {it}: pen_obj={best:.7f} wild={wild(P,L):.7f} d,sep,ov={constraints(P,L)}\", flush=True)\n    return x\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    n_sub = int(sys.argv[1]) if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 2\n    seed = int(sys.argv[2]) if len(sys.argv) > 2 else 0\n    t0 = time.time()\n    x = run(seed=seed, n_sub=n_sub)\n    L, pts = unpack(x); P = Polygon(pts)\n    d, sep, ov = constraints(P, L)\n    print(json.dumps(dict(n_sub=n_sub, seed=seed, L=L, wild=wild(P, L), diam=d, sep=sep, overlap=ov,\n                          feasible=bool(d <= 1+1e-9 and sep >= 1-1e-9 and ov <= 1e-12),\n                          vertices=pts.tolist(), time=time.time()-t0)))\n\ndef independent_check(P, L):\n    \"\"\"Union of all tiles clipped to a fundamental domain (parallelogram) vs 6*area(T).\"\"\"\n    from shapely.ops import unary_union\n    g1, g2 = LATT(L)\n    dom = Polygon([(0,0), tuple(g1), tuple(g1+g2), tuple(g2)])\n    tiles = [affinity.translate(rot(P, j), *lam) for j in range(6) for lam in [np.zeros(2)] + lattice_vecs(L, 3)]\n    cov = unary_union([t.intersection(dom) for t in tiles]).area\n    return cov / dom.area, 6*P.area/dom.area\n", "finalize.py": "\"\"\"Collect the optimizer outputs, restore strict feasibility by scaling each tile\nabout its centroid so that diam <= 1 - 1e-9, re-check all constraints with an\nindependent union-area computation, and report the best certified wild density.\"\"\"\nimport json, glob, math\nimport numpy as np\nfrom shapely.geometry import Polygon\nfrom shapely import affinity\nfrom optimize import constraints, wild, independent_check, diam\n\nrows = []\nfor fn in sorted(glob.glob('run_*.log')):\n    last = [l for l in open(fn) if l.startswith('{')]\n    if not last: continue\n    r = json.loads(last[-1])\n    P = Polygon(r['vertices']); L = r['L']\n    # scale to enforce diam <= 1 strictly; scaling about centroid keeps the tile inside\n    # a slightly shrunken copy of itself, which can only increase separations and\n    # cannot create overlaps with other tiles\n    f = min(1.0, (1 - 1e-9) / diam(P))\n    Q = affinity.scale(P, xfact=f, yfact=f, origin='centroid')\n    d, sep, ov = constraints(Q, L)\n    cov, six = independent_check(Q, L)\n    feas = Q.is_valid and d <= 1 and sep >= 1 and ov == 0.0 and abs(cov - six) < 1e-9\n    rows.append(dict(file=fn, n_vertices=len(r['vertices']), L=L, wild=1-cov, diam=d, sep=sep, overlap=ov,\n                     union_check=abs(cov-six), feasible=bool(feas), vertices=list(map(list, Q.exterior.coords))[:-1]))\nrows.sort(key=lambda r: r['wild'] if r['feasible'] else 9)\nfor r in rows:\n    print(f\"{r['file']:20s} n={r['n_vertices']:3d} L={r['L']:.6f} wild={r['wild']:.6f} 1/p={1/r['wild']:.2f} diam={r['diam']:.10f} sep={r['sep']:.6f} ov={r['overlap']:.1e} feasible={r['feasible']}\")\njson.dump(rows, open('results.json', 'w'), indent=1)\n", "results.json": "[{\"file\": \"run_sub2_s7.log\", \"n_vertices\": 16, \"L\": 1.9885609932831376, \"wild\": 0.02795703575506292, \"diam\": 0.9999949634740191, \"sep\": 1.001534181955326, \"overlap\": 0.0, \"union_check\": 1.1102230246251565e-16, \"feasible\": true, \"vertices\": [[0.3763436849700174, -0.21321536944840652], [0.5575984877782464, -0.3381027590917892], [0.7581582103273838, -0.4381810502735147], [0.934377353057864, -0.31312669510893765], [1.12086235946857, -0.2258923088827843], [1.140549783605837, -0.0025425130053637088], [1.120291576865768, 0.2135499368742614], [0.9586406789701025, 0.31358919376698985], [0.7585621173273205, 0.43745191721308785], [0.5750659595902687, 0.3154792099553819], [0.3831804094278215, 0.22423067027459573], [0.2931122024324324, 0.16015834921021704], [0.17915652474678098, 0.10900611516466198], [0.145284054464447, -0.006263308569330619], [0.19465683871873365, -0.10835168590003343], [0.2806976933322584, -0.1703960158141111]]}, {\"file\": \"run_sub2_s0.log\", \"n_vertices\": 16, \"L\": 1.9735629982641787, \"wild\": 0.02812515031215368, \"diam\": 0.9995371631240337, \"sep\": 1.0152074521517818, \"overlap\": 0.0, \"union_check\": 1.1102230246251565e-16, \"feasible\": true, \"vertices\": [[0.4009633852957236, -0.22984893520581987], [0.5600057056150823, -0.31973422677025937], [0.7819004386598282, -0.443288786467009], [0.9503988105290697, -0.31995536344206765], [1.115